WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.668
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)
-Okay, welcome to Overtime.

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:03.702
We're here
with Minnesota congressman

00:00:03.702 --> 00:00:05.938
and 2024 Democratic
presidential candidate,

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:07.006
Dean Phillips.

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:10.075
Host of<i> Fareed Zakaria GPS</i>
on CNN, Fareed Zakaria.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:12.946
And president of Eurasia Group
and GZERO Media, Ian Bremmer.

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:14.013
Here are the questions,

00:00:14.079 --> 00:00:15.381
I'm rushing
'cause I gotta get to Vegas.

00:00:15.514 --> 00:00:19.218
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)
-This is for you, Congressman.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.087
"Who would you choose
to be your running mate?"

00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:22.889
Oh, good question.
I didn't ask you that.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.958
Oh, I have to choose
a different person now?

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:26.993
-Uh. Well, your running mate.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:28.795
-My running mate?
-Yeah.

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:30.263
It's way too early for that.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:32.632
I will surprise you,
I promise you that.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:33.899
I promise you that.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:35.335
-Meaning? I don't--
-I will surprise you.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:37.736
I will absolutely surprise you
with a running mate.

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:38.938
FAREED ZAKARIA:
Good surprise or bad surprise?

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:41.007
-Good surprise.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:42.108
-BILL MAHER: Yeah, that's...
-Well--

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:44.410
It almost sounded like a threat.
(CHUCKLES)

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.780
-I promise you.
-Really?

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.682
-I will surprise you.
-It's not Carrot Top, is it?

00:00:49.748 --> 00:00:52.418
-(FAREED CHUCKLING)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, CHEERING)

00:00:52.484 --> 00:00:54.654
-(CHUCKLES) Carrot Top--
-All right.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.255
-Carrot--
-I love him, but I don't know.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.790
No, Carrot Top
had too high demands.

00:00:57.856 --> 00:00:58.958
-All right.
-I mean, I can't give away--

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.260
I can't give away
this stuff so early.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.428
-I know you want an answer,
I'm sorry.
-All right, did Democrats, uh,

00:01:02.494 --> 00:01:04.063
make a strategic error

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:07.232
by not saving Kevin McCarthy
now that we're stuck

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:09.602
with a much more extreme
Speaker of the House?

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.337
That's an interesting question.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.272
-Well, there really is--
-They could have, right?

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.040
There's a danger of a really...

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:16.542
I mean,
you were alluding to this.

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:19.178
Of a real political
constitutional crisis

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.013
'cause right,
Trump is gonna be the nominee.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.883
So, one of two things
are gonna happen in 2024.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.519 line:0%
He's either gonna win,
that has its own problems,

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.588 line:0%
-or he's gonna claim he won.
-DEAN PHILLIPS: Exactly.

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:30.189 line:0%
-Those are the only two options.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:01:30.255 --> 00:01:31.157 line:0%
-BILL: Absolutely.
-Right?

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:32.558 line:0%
BILL:
I've said it for seven years.

00:01:32.624 --> 00:01:34.694
-Right. And--
-But he's gonna show up...

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.562
-But this time--
-...Inauguration Day,

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:40.633
-January 2025, he will show up.
-But this time,

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.002
say the Pennsylvania state
legislature,

00:01:43.068 --> 00:01:44.436
where the laws, I think,
have been changed,

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:46.839
where they can send
an alternate, uh,

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:50.076
slate of electors,
and who do they send them to?

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.445
-The Speaker of the House.
-DEAN: Mm-hmm. Exactly.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.046
-Mike Johnson. Who is--
-BILL: Right.

00:01:54.279 --> 00:01:55.581
Who is gonna be very willing

00:01:55.647 --> 00:01:57.050
-to hear all the stuff...
-BILL: Right.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.751
...that at least Kevin McCarthy

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:00.119
-in the crunch...
-BILL: Right.

00:02:00.185 --> 00:02:01.421
-DEAN: And let me tell you guys.
-You know?

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.021
It's important
everybody know this.

00:02:03.188 --> 00:02:04.924
We extended
a number of overtures

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:07.559 line:0%
to Speaker McCarthy,
a number of other Republicans,

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:08.994 line:0%
saying we wanna work together.

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:11.096 line:0%
Just make
some modest concessions.

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:12.464 line:0%
First of all,
make the House work,

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:13.632 line:0%
that was our first demand.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:14.968 line:0%
Not one of them
would speak to us

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.702 line:0%
because they knew
if they actually attracted

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.171
a single Democratic vote,

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.139
-let alone ten, 15, 20...
-Right.

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:21.708
...that they
would be eviscerated

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.476
by their brothers and sisters
on their side.

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.178
That is the culture of Congress

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.346
that is absolutely destroying
the country.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.881
IAN BREMMER:
That's the culture of the House.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:30.349
-The culture of the House.
-Yes, not the Senate.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.917
DEAN: But no, it's not--
That is true, not the Senate.

00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:32.951
But that is the truth.

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:34.820
I heard you say before
when we were talking that,

00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:36.922
you know, you're gonna stop this
and we gotta work together.

00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:38.825
Everybody says that.
What's the plan?

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.693
-What's the plan to do that?
-Well, the plan is--

00:02:40.759 --> 00:02:43.096
You just said they wouldn't even
fucking talk to you.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:44.163
-IAN: What?
-I--

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:45.564
-What's the plan?
-No, no.

00:02:45.631 --> 00:02:49.569
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)
-Oh, no. No, no.

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:50.870
-FAREED: Well, it begins--
-No, let me--

00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:52.838
It begins
with the surprise running mate.

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:54.940
-Yes, that-- It begins with--
No, let me--
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:56.309
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.110
-I mean it. Look, as--
-Dick Cheney?

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:01.680
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-IAN: You said all parties.

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:03.583
-I was the most
bipartisan member of Congress...
-IAN: Team of rivals.

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:05.218
...last year,
the second most this year.

00:03:05.284 --> 00:03:07.987
I really do, I love my brothers
and sisters on both sides.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.056
There are
some wonderful Republicans,

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.124
who I think have a chance
to rise,

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:13.659
I think want to work together.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.328
This wasn't the time to do it,
but wish to do so

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:17.563
and there are some outstanding--

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.598
But again,
how do you liberate them

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:21.600
-from this problem
you're talking about...
-I'll tell you why.

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.169
-...where they're afraid to.
-That's why I'm running-- Look,

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.404
I'm running for president
to win.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:25.371
I believe we can.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.939
I believe it's time
for a new generation.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.842 line:0%
-Does anybody agree, by the way?
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.244 line:0%
And-- And...

00:03:33.278 --> 00:03:35.548 line:0%
You know, the last time
in American history

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.550 line:0%
that I think a president
really accomplished the notion

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:39.218
of a team of rivals
was Abe Lincoln.

00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:40.620
And I do think it's time,

00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:43.589
I really do believe it's time
for a Democratic president

00:03:43.789 --> 00:03:45.925
to ensure that there
are conservative voices

00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:48.327
in the White House,
within the Cabinet,

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:51.096
uh, having his or her ear,
and vice versa.

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.965
It should go the other way
as well. I'll do so.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:55.068
And I think so that's why
running for president,

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.036
you can actually break
this gridlock by actually...

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:58.704
-I think I know
what the surprise is.
-...engaging conservatives.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:03:59.872
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, CHEERING)
-IAN: Yeah?

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.307
-Oh, no, no. I didn't say that.
-No, no, no.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:02.775
But you're hinting
that you would have

00:04:02.841 --> 00:04:04.210
your team of rivals,
somebody else...

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:05.377
Oh, absolutely,
in the White House.

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:06.779
...so that your vice president
would be...

00:04:06.845 --> 00:04:07.847
No, I'm not saying I am.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:09.148
I'm saying
I would not rule that out.

00:04:09.214 --> 00:04:11.383
IAN: You're saying you might.
You're sort of teasing it.

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:13.752
-You're saying you might.
-BILL: Just say it, just say it.

00:04:13.852 --> 00:04:17.290
-It's Ramaswamy.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, CHEERING)

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:19.592
All right. That, I-- That...

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:22.395
I think I can promise you.
It ain't--

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:24.664
-It ain't Ramaswamy.
-But somebody like-- But, like--

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.666
All right, so we won't say
it's your VP.

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:29.736
But, like, who are some of
the more reasonable Republicans

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:32.104
who, if that was the direction
you were going into,

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.239
-you would choose from.
-Well first of all,

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:34.841
I think we lost two of
our great, young conservatives

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.142
in Anthony Gonzalez,
uh, Pete Meijer.

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:41.114
They had the audacity to vote
to impeach Trump, ten of them.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:43.282
Nine of them got thrown out
of the House essentially.

00:04:43.348 --> 00:04:45.017
I will tell you
that Dusty Johnson,

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:46.952
uh, a very principled,
good person--

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:48.420
-Dusty Johnson?
-Dusty Johnson.

00:04:48.487 --> 00:04:49.856
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-Who's that?

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.557
-(CHUCKLES)
-DEAN: See? You don't know.

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:52.792
-That's--
-I don't know. I thought he--

00:04:52.858 --> 00:04:54.894
I thought he was some
old Western actor, you know?

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.097
-Dusty Johnson. Remember--
-(SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

00:04:58.163 --> 00:04:59.531
-Remember Dusty Johnson?
-But nobody knows.

00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:01.700
-Yeah, no, nobody knows.
-You guys, nobody knows--

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:02.868
-Okay.
-Nobody knows--

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.104
He's gonna be
on the show next week. (LAUGHS)

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:06.672
(LAUGHS) Phillips, Johnson,
that's who I'm--

00:05:06.738 --> 00:05:09.542
See, if I out my friends,
they're gonna lose their races.

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:10.843
I don't wanna do it.
But very sincerely,

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:12.512
the problem is
they're the work horses,

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:14.013
not the show horses,
so you don't know their names.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.414
-BILL: Right.
-You know Lauren Boebert

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:16.582
and Marjorie Taylor Greene...

00:05:16.682 --> 00:05:17.783
-BILL: Yes, we do.
-...and Jim Jordan

00:05:17.849 --> 00:05:19.484
because they're destructive,

00:05:19.551 --> 00:05:21.620
-and I'm tired of it.
-How about Mitt Romney?

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:24.991
-Mitt Romney, he's a gentleman.
-He's a gentleman.

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:26.459
-And he's principled.
-(CHUCKLES)

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:27.859
And he already ran...

00:05:27.926 --> 00:05:29.294
-He already ran.
-...and he's a known quantity.

00:05:29.361 --> 00:05:30.896
I mean, yes,
a lot of people hate him,

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.699
-but, like-- No, but like...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:36.235
-But he stood...
-He stood strong.

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:37.569
He's one of those, what I call,

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:39.172
"As good
as it gets Republicans."

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:41.474
Liz Cheney, Liz--
I sat with Liz Cheney...

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:42.675
-Ah, they hate her.
-...on January 6th.

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:44.676
-They don't hate Mitt as much.
-They hate principle right now

00:05:44.743 --> 00:05:46.011
and it's a shame.
Liz Cheney had principles,

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:48.080
she got thrown out of the House.
I was with her on January 6th,

00:05:48.146 --> 00:05:49.748
when she looked
at the television screen,

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:50.749
Donald Trump on it.

00:05:50.849 --> 00:05:52.085
-She said, "He's responsible."
-BILL: Right.

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:53.085
"We're gonna hold him
to account."

00:05:53.218 --> 00:05:54.219
The whole room erupted.

00:05:54.419 --> 00:05:56.755
Democrats and Republicans.
A year later, look who was left.

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.257
-Very few.
-So, okay last question.

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:02.728
RFK is leading among, I read,
young people and independents

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:06.165
and in a three-way race, uh,
he gets now, like,

00:06:06.465 --> 00:06:07.567
-higher than, like--
-Twenty-two percent,

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:09.067
-apparently, in the last one.
-He gets 22. I mean,

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:10.736
that's pretty amazing,
what do you think?

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.304
Yeah, but he takes more
from Trump, all right?

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:13.839
-BILL: Takes more from Trump.
-Takes more from Trump, and,

00:06:13.905 --> 00:06:15.408
you know, I mean,
he's sort of dominating

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:16.876
the conspiracy theory lane,

00:06:16.942 --> 00:06:19.412 line:0%
which is a lane now
in US politics.

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:22.781 line:0%
Um, and if he continues to run
as opposed to, like,

00:06:22.848 --> 00:06:25.184 line:0%
the No Labels,
Joe Manchin fever dream,

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:26.953 line:0%
which I think
was never going to happen.

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:29.188
Um, then it actually gives Biden
more of a shot,

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:31.624
and at the end of the day,
if good Dean Phillips

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:33.893
doesn't somehow make it
to take Biden out,

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.562
um, then you're gonna need
to have Biden be able to do it

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:38.431
and a third-party candidate
may actually help on that front.

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:40.266
I mean, the fundamental problem,

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:42.101
why all of these scenarios
are terrifying,

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:44.503
is we don't actually have
a real election, right?

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.106
I mean, Biden will win
probably by nine million votes,

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:49.041
-but the most powerful man--
-BILL: Biden will?

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:50.776
-Right.
-IAN: Popular votes.

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:52.311
-Against Trump?
-Popular vote, right?

00:06:52.411 --> 00:06:53.379
-It doesn't mean anything?
-He won by--

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:54.847
He won by seven
and a half last time.

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:57.049
Oh, I'm glad you're so sanguine
about that. I am not.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.684
But what I'm not sanguine
about is--

00:06:58.750 --> 00:06:59.785
BILL: He could totally lose.

00:06:59.851 --> 00:07:01.287
No, but-- but even if--

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:03.088
If I didn't think he
was gonna lose, I wouldn't be

00:07:03.155 --> 00:07:04.256
all in for Dean Phillips.

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:08.360
-You're not listening.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING, CHEERING)

00:07:08.427 --> 00:07:10.496
Dean Phillips,
I've said it for years.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:12.498
(FAREED LAUGHING)

00:07:12.564 --> 00:07:14.734
For God's sake. Please.

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:16.902
-And if not him, Dusty Johnson.
-Get behind Phillips. Okay.

00:07:17.002 --> 00:07:18.871
No, but the point is,
it's gonna be decided

00:07:18.937 --> 00:07:20.439
in four states, right?

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:22.007
I mean, the Electoral College

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:23.442
-is what matters.
-BILL: Yeah. Yes.

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:25.678
Biden will win the popular vote,

00:07:25.745 --> 00:07:26.979
-the problem is...
-BILL: You don't know that.

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:28.414
...four states, Pennsylvania,

00:07:28.481 --> 00:07:30.382
-Arizona, Georgia, Wisconsin.
-He'll win the popular vote.

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:31.417
-Doesn't matter.
-And you're probably--

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:32.852
And he's down
in each of them, guys.

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:33.953
-Yeah. Yeah.
-He's down in each

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.454
of the battleground states
right now.

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:36.555
That's one reason
I'm doing this.

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:37.590
We have to do this.

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:39.258
-The alternative is disastrous.
-Okay, I gotta go to Vegas.

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:41.928
-Thank you very much everybody.
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)

